From 3e1de10cfdb5686d6b1c2221a9317c5d1e800fac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 12:48:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stage 283: does the tape survive its own growth

280 reached RAW_EXAM_OK on 187 addresses over 530 slots, and every number
in it is a statement about an index of 530 entries. The concept says the
mind does not grow with the knowledge, so the invariant can only fail on
the tape side - which means the question is answerable without training
anything, and a ladder that would take days with a mind attached takes
minutes without one.

Four numbers per rung, no policy, no BC, no RL. How much of a retrieved
list belongs to the address it was retrieved for. Whether the return path
still separates the value the corpus settled on from a value taken
elsewhere in the tape - measured as the distance between the two rates,
since a check that fires on everything is as useless as one that fires on
nothing, and both failures have already happened here. How close the
nearest other address key gets, because distinct entities crowd as the
tape fills. And the family mix with nothing quotaing it, since 280's tie
rate comes from --min-per-family and is not a fact about text.

Slopes are reported beside the gates. A metric that clears its floor
while falling steeply is the case that decides whether this scales or has
merely not broken yet.

